{
 "kind": "skeleton",
 "title": "A record and its setup",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail is open at a desktop and shut to its icons on a tablet, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. Every view shows the same record and the same setup; only the arrangement changes. The record is the page level: its picture, its name, and under the name its kind, its code and its owner, with its action at the end. Each part of the setup is a container, its title and its actions in its header; a container whose content is cards lets the cards stand on their own. Each thing set up is a card, with its own action at the end of its title. At a desktop the cards stand two across in the main column and the short part stands beside it; on a tablet and a phone all of it is one column. Each brand of the social sign-in is a tile as tall as a control: a person presses it to set it up, and a small check at its corner says it is set up. Registration closes the card, a line with the switch at its end. Who owns the record is a plain card in the short column under the web addresses, with the action that hands it over.",
 "layout": {
  "type": "RAIL",
